  <% if @name.category_for_edit.takes_parent_1? %>
    <%# Parent: powered by stimulus-autocomplete instead of the vendored
        typeahead.js/Bloodhound widget. Label, title, dom ids, param names
        and the input's classes are all kept as they were, so the GUI is
        unchanged; only the JS driving the dropdown is different.

        Server-side resolution (Name::AsResolvedTypeahead::ForParent) is
        untouched - it doesn't know or care which JS widget populated these
        fields.

        Which endpoint suggests the parents depends on the name's category,
        exactly as the three typeahead.js set-up calls this replaced did -
        see TypeaheadsHelper#parent_suggestions_url_for.

        live_params sends the rank currently chosen in the form's Rank
        select, which restricts which names can be a parent - the old
        Bloodhound sources read it out of the select the same way, on every
        keystroke, because the user can change rank without leaving the
        form.

        extra_params sends the name's own id as name_id, as those sources
        also did from the input's data-name-id attribute.

        term_delimiter keeps a pick from poisoning the next search: the
        suggestions read "<full name> | <rank> | <status> | <n> instances"
        and picking one puts all of that into the input. %>
    <% help_text = @name.category_for_edit.parent_1_help_text %>
    <div data-controller="name-parent-family"
         data-action="autocomplete.change->name-parent-family#sync">
      <%= render "shared/autocomplete_field",
                 f: f,
                 id_attribute: :parent_id,
                 input_id: "name-parent-typeahead",
                 input_name: "name[parent_typeahead]",
                 input_value: @name.parent.try("full_name"),
                 label: "#{"First " if @name.hybrid?}Parent",
                 label_suffix: (" [#{help_text}]" if help_text.present?),
                 required: @name.requires_parent_1?,
                 title: "Name parents will be suggested as you type, so please select from the list. Duplicates and names without instances are excluded.  Rank restrictions also apply.",
                 url: parent_suggestions_url_for(@name),
                 input_class: "requires-rank",
                 extra_params: { name_id: @name.id },
                 live_params: { rank_id: "name_name_rank_id" },
                 term_delimiter: "|" %>
      <%# Outside the field's own wrapper div: .autocomplete-results is
          positioned at top: 100% of that wrapper, so anything else inside
          it would push the suggestion dropdown down below it. %>
      <p>
        <span class="hide-if-rank <%= 'hidden' if @name.name_rank %>">
          Cannot be set if there is no rank.
        </span>
      </p>
    </div>
  <% end %>
